{
  "version": 2,
  "template": "bird",
  "space": "delta",
  "comment": "Troupe's clip library for the bird skeleton -- the winged archetype. Local joint rotations, XYZW. space=delta means each value is a rotation from the bone's own REST orientation, not the pose editor's node-local frame -- see blender_worker.POSE_SPACES. Every value was computed from a world-axis angle and converted through the bone's rest frame (basis = rest^-1 * R * rest): about world Y a positive angle drops the LEFT wing tip and about world Z a positive one sweeps it backward, and the right wing carries the mirror of the same world rotation. THE WINGS ARE POSED IN EVERY KEY OF EVERY CLIP, including the ones that never move them: the template's rest wing is fully spread, and in delta space a bone a key does not mention blends toward rest -- so a folded wing that goes unsaid in one key of a loop unfolds through the middle of it. walk is a real bird walk and not a hop: the leg chain (thigh/shin/foot) carries a 40-degree stride and the neck thrusts forward at each footfall and holds while the body catches up, which is the head-bob, running at twice the stride. jump is a take-off -- crouch, upstroke, the downstroke that does the lifting, then a glide -- because a winged family that cannot leave the ground is the one gap the archetype exists to fill. root_translation is in character-height units.",
